          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Global edtech funding collapses as investors pivot from K-12 apps to AI workforce training",
            "articleSection": "Education & Youth",
            "abstract": "Venture capital funding for K-12 education technology has dropped sharply worldwide, with investors redirecting capital toward AI-powered workforce training platforms that promise faster and more measurable returns. The shift is leaving school-focused edtech startups in emerging markets particularly exposed, as they had relied on international VC to reach underserved students. Rest of World's analysis shows the funding reorientation is accelerating a two-tier global education technology landscape.",
            "url": "https://restofworld.org/2026/edtech-funding-collapse-k12-startups-ai-workforce/",
            "publisher": {
              "@type": "NewsMediaOrganization",
              "name": "The AI Chronicle",
